DB_LOCK(3)

# NAME

db\_lock - RAII lock for package database directory

# SYNOPSIS

```
#include <libpkgcore/db_lock.h>

class db_lock {
public:
    db_lock(const std::string& root, bool exclusive = true);
    ~db_lock();
};
```

# DESCRIPTION

*db\_lock* provides scoped locking of the package database directory.

The lock is acquired during construction and released during
destruction. This enforces correct lock lifetime through object
scope.

The lock is applied to the directory specified by:

```
root + pkgutil::PKG_DIR
```

# SEMANTICS

- exclusive = true:
	exclusive lock, intended for mutation operations

- exclusive = false:
	shared lock, intended for read-only access

# ERRORS

Throws *std::runtime\_error* if:

- directory cannot be opened
- lock acquisition fails

# LIFETIME

The lock is held as long as the *db\_lock* object exists.

Destroying the object releases the lock.

# NOTES

This class relies on DIR\* and underlying filesystem semantics.
Behavior depends on platform locking guarantees.

# SEE ALSO

*fs\_utils*(3),
*pkgutil*(3),
*libpkgcore*(7)

